{"path":"string/multibyte/char16_t","title":"char16_t","titleHtml":"char16_t","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/string/multibyte/char16_t","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"char16_t is an unsigned integer type used for 16-bit wide characters and is the same type as uint_least16_t.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/string/multibyte\"><code>&lt;uchar.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-c11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw1\">typedef</span> <a href=\"/w/c/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw129\">uint_least16_t</span></a> char16_t<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c11\">(since C11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">char16_t</span></code> is an unsigned integer type used for 16-bit wide characters and is the same type as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw129\">uint_least16_t</span></a></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>On any given platform, by the definition of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><a href=\"/w/c/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw129\">uint_least16_t</span></a></span></code>, the width of type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">char16_t</span></code> can be greater than 16 bits, but the actual values stored in an object of type <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">char16_t</span></code> will always have a width of 16 bits.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;uchar.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> char16_t wcs<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> u<span class=\"st0\">\"zß水🍌\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// or \"z\\u00df\\u6c34\\U0001f34c\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/c/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw100\">size_t</span></a> wcs_sz <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span> wcs <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"kw4\">sizeof</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>wcs<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%zu UTF-16 code units: [ \"</span>, wcs_sz<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw100\">size_t</span></a> n <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> wcs_sz<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%#x \"</span>, wcs<span class=\"br0\">[</span>n<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw851\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"]<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>6 UTF-16 code units: [ 0x7a 0xdf 0x6c34 0xd83c 0xdf4c 0 ]</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.28 Unicode utilities &lt;uchar.h&gt; (p: 292)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.20.1.2 Minimum-width integer types (p: 212-213)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.28 Unicode utilities &lt;uchar.h&gt; (p: 398)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.20.1.2 Minimum-width integer types (p: 290)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.18.1.2 Minimum-width integer types (p: 256)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/types\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span><span>Fundamental types</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/multibyte","title":"Null-terminated multibyte strings"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"char16_t","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. char16_t is an unsigned integer type used for 16-bit wide characters and is the same type as uint_least16_t."},{"label":"Notes","note":"On any given platform, by the definition of uint_least16_t, the width of type char16_t can be greater than 16 bits, but the actual values stored in an object…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":["C11"],"wordCount":177,"codeBlockCount":2}
